architecture close-consequence
  canonical_name CloseConsequence
  family economic
  domain Economic
  maturity measured
  semantic_question What would change if this reconciliation were applied, and what does the system of record actually say is outstanding?
  # A consequential financial write should be evaluable before it is authorised.
  # "If we allocate this payment, which obligations close and what moves" has an
  # exact answer needing no effect at all, so it is computed on the pure tier and
  # nothing here writes anything. The engine produces a consequence; applying it
  # is a separate act behind an authority the engine does not hold.
  node_types ReconciliationObligation
  node_types PaymentAllocation
  node_types Consequence
  edge_types reconciles
  edge_types allocated_from
  state_types open
  state_types reconciled
  state_types unevaluable
  invariant the engine computes consequences and never applies them; no write occurs on this path and the receipt says so
  invariant an obligation the estate cannot resolve is reported unevaluable and never counted as closable; treating an unknown amount as closable is how a close report overstates what was reconciled
  invariant over-allocation and under-allocation are carried per obligation and reported beside the net; a single net figure hides that money is missing in both directions
  invariant a reconciliation formula is validated against the population before it is believed; summing the gross fee overstated one payment fifty-fold, and only the allocated portion reconciles
  invariant financial closure is money work, so it runs on the exact representation and where the data already lives, whatever loss budget is offered
  forbidden_inference a computed consequence -> an approval
  forbidden_inference a closable obligation -> a closed one
  forbidden_inference an amount observed in the mirror -> the amount the source holds
  computational_form derivation
  native_format json
  invariant the receipt says whether the system of record was reached, because an empty answer from a database that replied and an empty answer from one that refused the connection were the same dict; every obligation then read "the system of record returned no row for it" while the client had never connected
  invariant a failed query is not an empty result; the client's exit status is checked and its error carried, and only the error line, which names the host and the failure and no credential
  invariant no direction is claimed while the source is unreachable, and the suite asserts that absence rather than demanding a distinction the run could not compute
  forbidden_inference an unreachable system of record -> an obligation that cannot reconcile
  source_path scripts/product_close_consequence.mjs
  source_path scripts/product_close_consequence.py.archive
  source_path packs/upper90/product-contract-ai-loss.yaff
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/close_consequence_test.sh
  witness scripts/tests/product_close_consequence.test.mjs
  invariant the active consequence reader uses read-only SQLite and a read-only MySQL query; failed source access stays unevaluable and no credential value is emitted in the receipt
  measured AmountLeft = PayAmt - SUM(PaySpltAIAmt WHERE Active=1) reconciles 5917 of 9982 payments to exactly zero with $0.01 residual across all of them, which is what validates it
  measured the 101 tracked obligations are all unreconciled: 86 under-allocated and 15 over-allocated, net $325,790.01 outstanding
  measured across the whole payment population 3804 payments are under-allocated by $148,971,278.17 and 246 over-allocated by $326,832.81, so the tracked obligations cover 2.5% of the unreconciled set
  known_gap the mirror held financial events for 61 of 101 obligations while the source answers for all 101; the oracle store is a partial copy and its gaps read as unevaluable rather than as absent facts
  invariant the machinery is given a namespace, discovers the pack that namespace declares, and reads the reconciliation law that pack states; it holds no product's tables, columns, identifier prefix or schema string
  invariant a product is added by writing a pack and a namespace entry, never by adding another compiled code path; the first version carried one product's grammar in its filename, its SQL, its defaults and its schema version
  invariant a table or column arriving from a declaration is checked against a plain identifier shape before it reaches a query; a contract is content, and content must not be able to write SQL
  forbidden_inference a law read from a contract -> a law anyone validated (the pack records its own witness for that)
  known_gap the $148.9M under-allocated figure is a reconciliation position and not a claim about owed money; a payment received and not yet allocated is unreconciled without anything being wrong

architecture funding-closure
  canonical_name FundingClosure
  family economic
  domain Economic
  maturity measured
  semantic_question What prevents every plausible funding path from closing, and which of those obstacles is actually about money?
  # The wrong question is who will fund this, and the wrong answer is DECLINED. A
  # decline collapses a dozen separable conditions into one word, and they are not
  # the same kind of problem: one is cheaply resolvable, one needs a partner, one
  # needs time, and only some need capital. Keeping them apart is what makes the
  # remainder actionable rather than a number to raise.
  node_types FundingRequirement
  node_types FundingResidual
  node_types InstitutionalCapacity
  edge_types satisfies
  edge_types resolvable_by
  state_types SATISFIED
  state_types MISSING
  state_types UNKNOWN
  invariant the output is a classified remainder and never a verdict; each unmet condition carries the class of thing that would resolve it and the reason it is unmet
  invariant only one residual class is answered with money; collapsing the classes makes every shortfall look like a financing problem when most of them are evidence, partner or time
  invariant capacity is scoped to the institution that holds it; capital observed for one institution is not available to another, and a ceiling summed across institutions reports capacity that cannot be drawn
  invariant demand is counted at every publication status and the states are reported apart; filtering to published reported zero demand beside a ceiling that had counted it, and an expression of interest is not a commitment
  invariant an external capital market that has not been asked is unmeasured and contributes no amount, and it names the rung it stopped at; the same ladder as every other market in this estate
  forbidden_inference a satisfied requirement -> funding
  forbidden_inference a residual -> a loan that must be raised
  forbidden_inference an unmeasured market -> an absent one
  forbidden_inference declared demand -> committed demand
  computational_form derivation
  native_format json
  source_path scripts/funding-closure.mjs
  source_path scripts/funding-residuals.cue
  source_path scripts/funding_closure.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/grant-closure.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/economic-reports.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/economic_reports.test.mjs runs the grant diagnostic shell without Python, preserves historical counters and explicitly labels their tag-presence, file-presence and declared-depth basis; malformed and oversized evidence cannot replace the prior report
  known_gap the retained-grant diagnostic is not the verified funding-closure owner: attestation presence verifies no signature, generic evidence verifies no grant-specific sufficiency, and absent listed residuals establish neither eligibility nor freshness
  witness scripts/tests/funding-closure.test.mjs proves institution-scoped demand includes drafts without cross-institution capital transfer and untried capital routes remain unmeasured; one-time complete receipt comparison against the former Python owner passed except timestamp
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/funding_closure_test.sh
  measured institution:nightgrid declares $6,063.00 of demand across 65 requests, all drafted and none committed; of 8 requirements 3 are satisfied and the remaining 5 classify as 1 capital, 2 evidence, 1 partner and 1 market
  known_gap TemporalCeiling is unmeasured because no requirement carries an observed_at, so nothing can be said about whether its evidence is still fresh enough to rely on
  known_gap no provider_route declares a capital capability, so the external capital market has never been named or asked; measuring it is the same trial machinery the retrieval market already uses
  known_gap a source this entry named could not be opened from this checkout -- /var/lib/bonfyre/cms/content-types/funding_requirement.json. The line is removed rather than repointed to something that merely looks similar, and what remains listed is the evidence this architecture actually stands on.
architecture funding-frontier
  canonical_name FundingFrontier
  family economic
  domain Economic
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Which combinations of capital routes would close, and what single condition is the most capital waiting on?
  # Routes are not alternatives to pick between. One form of capital routinely
  # satisfies the condition that unlocks a much larger one, so a grant and a
  # landlord contribution closing an equity condition can make a bank facility
  # executable -- three small closures unlocking a rail an order of magnitude
  # bigger. A list of lenders cannot express that; a combination search over
  # routes and the conditions they satisfy can.
  #
  # The search is pure: no capital moves, nothing is applied for, and no route is
  # contacted, so it runs on the pure tier under the same admission as any money
  # work.
  node_types FundingRoute
  node_types FundingWorld
  node_types ClosureHypothesis
  edge_types requires
  edge_types satisfies
  edge_types unlocks
  state_types EVIDENCED
  state_types UNKNOWN
  state_types BLOCKED
  invariant a route carries both what it requires and what it satisfies, and closure is computed to a fixed point because one route unlocking another can unlock a third
  invariant EVIDENCED, UNKNOWN and BLOCKED are kept apart and never collapsed; reporting unknown capacity as zero understates the frontier and sends a planner looking for money it may already reach, and reporting it as capacity is worse
  invariant a closure hypothesis is a recomputation of the whole world set with the condition treated as met, never an estimate of what it might unlock
  invariant satisfying a condition never removes a reachable world, and a run where it does is a bug in the closure rather than a finding
  invariant the frontier is computed and never acted on; no route is contacted and no application is made
  forbidden_inference a closing combination -> funding
  forbidden_inference an unblocked route -> an offer
  forbidden_inference UNKNOWN capacity -> zero capacity
  forbidden_inference an evidenced ceiling -> money that can be drawn today
  computational_form derivation
  native_format json
  source_path scripts/funding-frontier.mjs
  source_path scripts/funding_frontier.py.archive
  witness scripts/tests/funding-frontier.test.mjs proves bitset combination closure preserves route-unlocking, unknown capacity and pure effect boundaries; one-time complete receipt comparison against the former Python owner passed except timestamp
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/funding_frontier_test.sh
  measured 6 declared routes over institution:nightgrid produce 63 combinations of which 1 has no blocked route; revenue-history blocks a route in 96 of them, and the three backends of the pure tier agree that exactly 1 world survives
  measured the capital condition unlocks nothing on its own: cash-position and external-capital-route each gain zero worlds, while two cheaply-resolvable evidence conditions and one partner condition each gain two
  invariant an evidence artifact is priced against every route that requires it, not against one; a revenue history is one artifact three routes each need, and costing it against a single route understates it by however many others were waiting
  measured revenue-history is required by 3 of 6 declared routes and approved-demand by 2, so the two cheapest conditions to resolve are also the most reused
  known_gap five of six routes carry UNKNOWN capacity because no capital provider has been asked; measuring them is the same trial machinery the retrieval market already uses, and until then the evidenced ceiling is the only figure that means anything
  known_gap a source this entry named could not be opened from this checkout -- /var/lib/bonfyre/cms/content-types/funding_route.json. The line is removed rather than repointed to something that merely looks similar, and what remains listed is the evidence this architecture actually stands on.

architecture funding-prospect-frontier
  canonical_name FundingProspectFrontier
  family economic
  domain Economic / Funding discovery
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Which publicly observable funding opportunities are currently adjacent to programmes the estate is actually running, and what does each observation still not establish?
  purpose A read-only projection over the published ProgrammeFabric funding work packages and public Grants.gov Applicant API results. It makes the estate's real programmes discoverable to a funder or partner without calling a prospect an eligible application, an award, available money, or spend authority.
  consumes ProgramFabric
  consumes ForeignObservation
  publishes FundingProspectFrontier
  internal_calculus Every published ProgramInstance contributes only its published FundingWorkPackages. Each distinct declared rail is translated to public-catalogue search vocabulary, observed through the no-auth Grants.gov API, bounded to compact opportunity discovery fields, and rendered beside the unmodified programme declaration. The canonical rail remains visible beside its query vocabulary.
  invariant a declared funding rail is retained separately from the public query vocabulary used to discover it
  invariant the projection retains provider result count, observation time, endpoint, compact opportunity identity, provider status and response digest; it retains no API response token, applicant payload or submission credential
  invariant unavailable or empty public search is visible as an observation state and never contributes a zero-dollar or no-funding conclusion
  invariant public catalogue ordering is not eligibility; bounded lexical ordering only makes exact declared vocabulary results easier to inspect
  forbidden_inference a funding work package -> eligibility, application, award, available money, authority to submit or authority to spend
  forbidden_inference a public opportunity -> fit, eligibility, an application, award, available money or authority to submit
  forbidden_inference a missing or unavailable provider observation -> no funding exists
  computational_form projection
  native_format json
  source_path scripts/bootstrap_funding_frontier.py.archive
  source_path scripts/bootstrap_funding_frontier.mjs
  source_path scripts/publish_estate.sh
  witness scripts/tests/bootstrap-funding-frontier.test.mjs proves the Bun offline compiler retains the ProgrammeFabric declaration and human-line boundary; scripts/tests/bootstrap_funding_observation_test.sh proves bounded live-shaped observations retain a response digest, reorder lexical matches and mark a provider failure unavailable without a funding verdict
  source_path scripts/tests/bootstrap_funding_observation_test.sh
  measured 2026-09-25 the full published estate contributed 10 ProgramInstances and 31 separately scoped FundingWorkPackages over 23 declared rails; all 23 were observed through the public Grants.gov Applicant API and yielded a bounded 73-record discovery frontier without any application or payment effect
  known_gap catalogue vocabulary alone produces generic false-adjacent results for several legacy rail names; opportunity-specific eligibility and programme fit must be observed and compiled before any route is promoted beyond discovery
architecture capital-transformation-network
  canonical_name CapitalTransformationNetwork
  family economic
  domain Economic
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Given what this institution holds, which ordered compositions of capital transformations are structurally permitted, and what does it hold at the end of each?
  # A financing product list has one row per instrument and a label saying what
  # the instrument supplies. Three things do not survive that shape: what the
  # instrument does to the state (a vendor term supplies no cash and moves an
  # outflow), which instruments cannot be held at once (rights compose; rows do
  # not), and which orders are permitted (a set has no order to be wrong about).
  # Writing each route as a transformation over the financial state keeps all
  # three, and turns the question from which product to which ordered path.
  node_types CapitalTransformation
  node_types FinancialState
  node_types CapitalPath
  edge_types requires
  edge_types consumes
  edge_types provides
  edge_types conflicts_with
  state_types admissible
  state_types refused
  state_types stranded
  invariant effects are not monotone, so there is no fixed point to compute; a transformation spends cash, dilutes ownership and consumes collateral-free, and closure algebra over removal would return one arbitrary order and present it as the answer
  invariant an unknown cash effect poisons the running total rather than contributing zero to it; a path with one unpriced step has an unknown end cash and cannot be said to reach anything
  invariant opening cash is evidenced internal capacity and nothing else; the requirement-satisfaction ceiling is a different quantity, and read as money it opened a $0 institution $6,063 up against a $6,074 target
  invariant a pair is mutually exclusive only where each is separately admissible and neither order of the two is; unreachability is not exclusion, and conflating them manufactured twelve collisions out of one missing token
  invariant reversibility belongs to the path at the position of its first irreversible step, because everything after that point can be unwound and nothing before it can
  invariant a counterfactual saturated state may be searched, and its findings are reported in their own section and never merged with what the institution can reach
  forbidden_inference an admissible path -> an available one
  forbidden_inference an unknown cash effect -> a zero one
  forbidden_inference a ranked path -> a recommended one; the ranking is a declared preference
  forbidden_inference structural admissibility -> a counterparty willing to transact
  forbidden_inference no admissible path containing both -> a conflict between the two
  computational_form search
  native_format json
  source_path scripts/capital_transform.mjs
  witness scripts/capital_transform.test.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/capital_transform_test.sh
  measured 11 declared transformations over institution:nightgrid, 1,111 ordered paths at depth 3: 141 admissible, 970 refused, 0 known to reach the declared $6,074 of demand because every capital-bearing step carries an UNKNOWN capacity
  measured bank-debt is stranded in every path, blocked on external-capital-route -- an unasked market rather than a credit judgement; its two declared rights conflicts are therefore with a route nothing can reach
  measured the reach report puts a grant three acts and 3.25 months out and equipment-lease two acts and 3 months out, so the binding constraint under this institution is elapsed time to evidence revenue, not selection among instruments
  measured the survivor predicate over the 141 paths was agreed by four independent reducers -- reference, hvm2, hvm4 and bend -- at 40 paths conceding no right and fully reversible
  known_gap every capital-bearing transformation carries an UNKNOWN cash delta, so the network answers which compositions are permitted and cannot answer how much any of them would raise

architecture route-arbitrage
  canonical_name RouteArbitrage
  family economic
  domain Economic / Routing
  layer economic
  semantic_question For a need this estate can serve from something it reads for nothing, what does the market charge for the same need?
  purpose The AddressPlane already decides which candidates serve a need. What it never knew is what each one costs. The estate holds 211 metered x402 sources and 2,291 sources it has proven it can read for nothing under a published permission, and both populations answer the same coordinates -- 137 metered sources answer affordance:search and 225 proven-free ones answer it too. A router that does not know this pays for an answer it could have had for free.
  maturity measured
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/price-book.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/route-arbitrage.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/economic-views.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tests/economic_views_test.mjs
  invariant the Bun economic projection atomically replaces its report only after successful bounded regular-file reads; route-owner failures remain explicit failed_route_reads rather than disappearing from coverage
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/economic_views_test.mjs invokes both economic shell entrypoints against temporary SQLite and retained bodies without Python or network; quoted prices preserve legacy evidence digests and base-unit scaling, thin markets and rounded-to-zero medians are refused, and mocked native Finance registration is never reported as sale or revenue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/route_cost_test.sh
  consumes CandidateAdvertisement
  publishes RankedCandidateFrontier
  internal_calculus the price book is read from bodies the sweep already retained rather than fetched. 211 metered sources were observed, three answered with an HTTP 402 payment envelope and the rest answered 200 because the paid endpoint is a deeper path and what was served was the service describing itself. Those descriptions carry prices; 39 carry a structured price field
  internal_calculus the spread is registered in BonfyreFinance rather than reported beside it. That owner already models a service as a buy price, a sell price and a source, ranks spreads and reports margin; a second pricing report would be a second vocabulary for one fact
  internal_calculus what routing avoids is a range and not a number. A router that does not know the prices does not pick the cheapest metered source, it picks one, so the expected avoidance is the mean of the metered options and reporting only the floor understates it by the width of the span
  invariant a published price wins over a free read of the same origin. Every metered service serves its own description for nothing, so the estate holds a proven free read of the landing page of something it has never paid for; counting that as evidence the service is free removed every priced source from the metered side of the route
  invariant dollars and base units are never compared. A price field carrying $0.005 is dollars and an amount field carrying 20000 is USDC at six decimals, which is two cents; read as dollars it becomes twenty thousand and a router would refuse a two-cent call as if it cost more than a car
  invariant a source nobody has read and nobody has priced is unknown, not free, and is never offered as a route
  cannot_infer a spread -> revenue; nobody was charged, nobody paid, and the sell price is what other services publish rather than a price anyone agreed with this estate
  cannot_infer cheapest -> best or adequate; whether a free source answers the question as well as a metered one is a judgement no price contains, and the exact verifier still decides
  cannot_infer a registered service -> a service anyone has asked for
  cannot_infer a published price -> a contracted rate, or a price that will still hold tomorrow
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/route_cost_test.sh runs on every build and holds the two mistakes that make this dangerous rather than merely wrong: two cents expressed in base units stays two cents, and a priced source whose landing page was read for free stays on the metered side
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/route-liveness.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/project-liveness.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/project_liveness_test.mjs runs the liveness shell with isolated receipts and mocked probes, preserves still-answering versus changed versus unavailable states, reports missing or invalid receipts and failed probes, and atomically emits a bounded deterministic host-balanced sample without live rereads
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/results/2026-09-13-route-economics.json
  invariant a spread is registered against a median and never a mean, and never against a market of fewer than four sellers. One source asks 149 dollars where most ask half a cent; the mean reported six dollars of avoidance on a coordinate whose median is five thousandths of one, and on a three-seller coordinate it reported 49 dollars against a 40 cent median
  internal_calculus per-call arbitrage is not the asset. Routing avoids roughly half a cent in a market deep enough to price, and nothing is built on undercutting half a cent. The asset is the table: 2,344 sources proven readable under a published permission, with digests, across 83 coordinates, and what it is worth is how fresh it is
  cannot_infer a registered spread -> demand; the estate's demand tables are empty and nobody has asked for anything
  witness the live estate registers 35 services across 83 coordinates after thin markets are refused, typical spread half a cent per call, with zero jobs logged and zero revenue
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tools/route-liveness.sh asked 60 routed sources again, one per host: 33 answered with the same digest, 15 answered with new content, 12 did not answer. The table is 80 percent routable and a quarter of its content moved inside a day, which is the number that makes an index worth maintaining rather than worth building once
  known_gap the liveness measure is a 60-source sample of a 2,344-source table and characterises the sample it drew
  known_gap 57 metered sources publish a price only as prose, such as a range in marketing copy, and are deliberately not parsed into a quote. 106 publish no price at all. The book covers 39 of 211
  known_gap nothing has been sold. 74 spreads are registered and BonfyreFinance reports no jobs and no margin, which is the honest state: opportunities ranked, nothing transacted

architecture demand-book
  canonical_name DemandBook
  family economic
  domain Economic / Demand
  layer economic
  semantic_question What is the machine-readable internet asking to be given, and which of it does this estate hold?
  purpose The estate's demand tables were empty and the conclusion drawn was that nobody was asking. What was true is that 3,316 primary URLs had been swept and every one of them returned a landing page -- what a service says about itself to a person. The asking happens somewhere else. A service that wants to be called by an agent publishes openapi.json, /.well-known/x402 or an agent card, and those declare field by field exactly what must be supplied to call it. That is demand: standing, published, machine-readable and free to read.
  maturity measured
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/discovery-sweep.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/demand-match.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/project-demand.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tests/project_demand_test.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/project_demand_test.mjs runs the live automation entrypoint against temporary retained declarations and ForeignTwin evidence without Python or network, preserves credential and payment-carrier distinctions, and never equates fillable input with authorization or payment
  consumes ForeignTwin
  publishes CapabilityDemand
  internal_calculus the discovery probe goes through the same observer as any other read, so robots is preflighted per path and a receipt with a digest is written for each. The twin id stays the occurrence's own, because this is another observation of the same thing at a path it publishes for exactly this purpose
  internal_calculus supply is what this estate can put on the wire and nothing else. A caller-supplied argument is not supply, and a credential is never ours to give -- 16 services ask only for tokens, keys, wallets or signatures and are recorded as unfillable rather than as demand met
  invariant capability/eligible needs a discriminator or it is a restatement of qualified. Every advertisement carries a lowerer, so having one separated nothing and the rung was refused; a declared input this estate can fill separates 44 services from 45, which is what makes it a rung rather than a relabelling
  cannot_infer a declared input -> this service asking this estate for it; the declaration is addressed to whoever reads it
  cannot_infer eligible -> authorized or activated; nobody has called anything and nobody has granted anything
  cannot_infer fillable -> adequate; the service still decides what it accepts
  witness the discovery sweep probed 446 paths across 209 hosts and retained 224 declarations, a 50 percent hit rate against a population where the landing-page sweep had found 16
  witness 89 services declare required inputs across 6,774 declared operations; 44 ask for something this estate demonstrably holds, the largest single ask being a URL, of which it holds 2,344 proven readable under a published permission with a digest each
  known_gap the estate probes two paths per source and there are more: /.well-known/mcp.json, /.well-known/ai-plugin.json and /llms.txt all appeared in the operation lists and none were swept
  internal_calculus a credential is four problems wearing one word, and treating them as one turned a decomposition into a shrug. A public identifier is published on purpose -- an x402 payTo is a destination and is meaningless if secret -- so it needs a declaration and not a secret store. A signature is produced by a key this estate holds. An issued token needs a registration, which is a commitment a person makes. And a keyless service needs none of it, which is what x402 was built for
  invariant the estate does not classify an address or a payTo as a secret. Doing so counted 29 of 38 credential asks as unsolvable when what they need is one institutional identity that a person chooses
  cannot_infer a blocked credential class -> an unsolvable one; each of the three has a different and named fix
  known_gap the issued class needs 19 registrations and every one of them is a commitment a person makes rather than a capability this estate can add
  known_gap github.com carries 2,670 of the MCP occurrences because their primary_url is a repository rather than an endpoint. The per-host cap removed them and the service behind each repository was never reached

architecture institution-identity
  canonical_name InstitutionIdentity
  family identity
  domain Identity / Attestation
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Who says this, and can anyone but us check it?
  purpose The estate holds tens of thousands of evidence rows and every one carries digests. A digest says the bytes did not move. It does not say who produced them, so until now every claim the estate made was checkable by the estate and by nobody else. An identity key closes that: a detached Ed25519 signature over the evidence digest makes the whole chain verifiable by anyone holding the published public key.
  maturity measured
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSign/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSign/tests/sign_test.sh
  publishes SignedAttestation
  internal_calculus real Ed25519 through libsodium, kept in its own binary. libbonfyre is linked by every other organ and does not acquire a signing dependency it does not need
  internal_calculus the signature is detached and taken over the content digest rather than the body, because the evidence file is twenty-three megabytes and the assertion is the same at a size anyone can carry
  invariant this is an identity and attestation key. It is not a payment key, holds no funds, authorizes no transfer, and is deliberately not the key an x402 payment would be signed with; one key holding both powers is how an attestation becomes a withdrawal
  invariant keygen refuses to replace an identity that already exists, because a regenerated key silently invalidates every signature the previous one made
  invariant the secret is created at 0600 and never exists at any wider mode, not even for the moment between creation and chmod
  cannot_infer a valid signature -> a true statement; it says this estate made the statement and that the bytes have not moved since
  cannot_infer an attestation -> a payment authorization
  witness cmd/BonfyreSign/tests/sign_test.sh proves both directions rather than one. A stub that rejects everything passes a test that only checks bad signatures are refused, which is exactly what the previous implementation would have done, so this asserts that a real signature verifies and that a tampered file, a tampered signature and a different key each do not
  witness the estate's 23MB evidence file is signed and verifies against the published public key alone
  known_gap bf_crypto still carries the symmetric tag under names borrowed from a public-key scheme. Its header now says what it implements and nothing calls it, but the functions remain and the honest fix is to delete them rather than document them
  known_gap the institution publishes an identity key and no payment address. That is a separate declaration with separate consequences and it is not made here

architecture served-answer
  canonical_name ServedAnswer
  family economic
  domain Economic / Service
  layer economic
  semantic_question Can this estate answer a request, or can it only describe one?
  purpose Everything before this measured. The estate observed 3,316 sources, closed 2,344 obligations, priced 39 metered services, matched 44 declared demands and signed its own evidence, and served nobody -- which made all of it an instrument reporting on itself. This takes a need, routes it to the cheapest source the estate has proven it can read, fetches the answer now, and returns the bytes with the chain that justifies them.
  maturity measured
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/serve.mjs
  consumes RankedCandidateFrontier
  publishes ServedAnswer
  internal_calculus the route is the cheapest candidate proven readable and never the cheapest candidate. A source nobody has read is not cheap, it is unknown, and it is not offered
  internal_calculus the answer carries a freshness verdict rather than a promise: unchanged means the bytes still hash to what was observed, changed means the source is live and has moved, unreachable means the table is wrong about it. Three of the first five answers came back changed, which is what a live source does
  internal_calculus every served answer is signed, so a caller can check who produced the routing decision without holding anything but the published key; the native entrypoint refuses a readable route if the institution key or signer is absent and publishes no answer on signer failure
  internal_calculus the native entrypoint binds a proven route to a parameterized occurrence lookup, retains the exact fetched bytes under their digest, and publishes a digest-named answer receipt and signature without invoking Python
  invariant a coordinate with no proven-readable source returns a refusal and not a guess; domain:law was refused on the first run for exactly that reason
  cannot_infer an answer -> a correct answer; it is what the routed source said when asked
  cannot_infer a routed source -> the best source; it is the cheapest one proven readable, and the exact verifier still decides
  cannot_infer a logged job -> revenue; five jobs are logged at zero cost and zero sold, because the estate paid nothing and nobody paid it
  witness five of six coordinates served end to end, each returning bytes, a route, a frontier count, the metered alternatives it avoided and a freshness verdict, every one signed and independently verifiable
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/serve_native_test.mjs proves the route-cost command arguments, quoted occurrence identity lookup, exact body digest, signature over the receipt, and refusal without proven read or signer
  known_gap nobody has asked. The jobs are logged against needs this estate chose to demonstrate, not requests anyone made, and margin is zero because nothing was sold rather than because pricing failed
  known_gap there is no served endpoint. The estate answers when invoked locally and publishes nothing an external caller could reach
  known_gap the native entrypoint has fixture parity witnesses but the five historical live answers have not been replayed through it; this change does not establish a public buyer or endpoint

architecture rate-discovery
  canonical_name RateDiscovery
  family economic
  domain Economic / Public price statements
  layer economic
  semantic_question Did an endpoint state a usable rate, and did the native Meter actually admit it?
  purpose Probe already-known API-shaped endpoints under their robots policy, distinguish a stated HTTP 402 amount from a Meter rate, and ask the native Meter to admit only an amount with qualified denomination and evidence.
  maturity implemented
  source_path scripts/sweep-rates.mjs
  source_path scripts/rate-discovery.cue
  source_path scripts/public-source-fetch.mjs
  consumes PriceSource
  publishes RateAdmissionAttempt
  internal_calculus a 402 response is a source observation; maxAmountRequired and crypto-asset amounts may be base-unit quantities and cannot become decimal Meter rates without denomination evidence, so this lowering admits only explicit fiat amounts under the declared currency list
  invariant a 402 alone does not increment the admitted count; only a successful native Meter command does
  forbidden_inference a 402 price statement -> a rate, payment commitment, settlement, or buyer quote
  forbidden_inference a Meter rate admitted here -> usage, accrual, or revenue
  witness scripts/tests/sweep_rates.test.mjs covers HTTP 402 extraction, source-scoped robots, parameterized endpoint selection, explicit base-unit refusal, and a native Meter admission count that follows the command result
  known_gap the native discovery has fixture witnesses but no fresh live endpoint replay; a source can change its schema, robots posture or quotation at any time
